{"id": "20517078", "revid": "359672", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20517078", "title": "Tom Sewell (cricketer, born 1806)", "text": "Thomas Sewell (5 May 1806 \u2013 1 November 1888) was an English professional cricketer whose career spanned the years 1830 to 1853. He was a right-handed batsman, occasional wicket-keeper and slow underarm bowler who was mainly associated with Surrey. He represented the Players in the Gentlemen v Players series and was an original member of William Clarke's All-England Eleven in 1846. His brother, William Sewell, played twice for Surrey, and his son, also named Tom Sewell, played for Surrey and the All-England Eleven."}
