{"id": "20517187", "revid": "11487766", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20517187", "title": "2002\u201303 Cardiff City F.C. season", "text": "During the 2002\u201303 season Cardiff City played in the Football League Division Two. They finished in six place and were promoted to Division One after beating Queens Park Rangers in the play-off final in Cardiff.\nThe season also saw Robert Earnshaw break the 56-year record of 30 league goals held by Stan Richards and the record of Hughie Ferguson of 32 goals in all competitions."}
{"id": "20517199", "revid": "41796233", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20517199", "title": "Preston Elliott", "text": "Preston Elliott (May 1, 1875 \u2013 January 12, 1939) was a Canadian farmer and politician from Ontario. Born in Chesterville, Ontario to William Elliott and Mary Agnes Rae, he served in the House of Commons of Canada for the Dundas electoral district as a member of the Progressive party. He was elected in 1921, but was defeated in the 1925 federal election. He was a Progressive candidate in 1926 and a Liberal in 1935, but lost both attempts at re-election. He was a member of the Ginger Group."}
